/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 83 0 R
/T (For a long time, humanity believed the universe was static eternal and unchanging. Yet, a few curious minds dared to question this still image of existence: Could a universe so vast truly be motionless? Or was there something deeper, hidden within the fabric of space itself, that we had yet to understand ?.As the 20th century unfolded, everything changed. Thanks to remarkable advances in astronomy and the study of light from distant galaxies, scientists discovered that space is not static but expanding and it has been doing so since its very beginning, around 13.8 billion years ago, according to the Big Bang theory. This revelation transformed our understanding of the cosmos. Galaxies and stars are not fixed in place; they are moving away from each other in a coordinated, measurable pattern. This was not speculation it was a conclusion drawn from precise observational evidence that reshaped modern cosmology.)
/E (For a long time, humanity believed the universe was static eternal and unchanging. Yet, a few curious minds dared to question this still image of existence: Could a universe so vast truly be motionless? Or was there something deeper, hidden within the fabric of space itself, that we had yet to understand ?.As the 20th century unfolded, everything changed. Thanks to remarkable advances in astronomy and the study of light from distant galaxies, scientists discovered that space is not static but expanding and it has been doing so since its very beginning, around 13.8 billion years ago, according to the Big Bang theory. This revelation transformed our understanding of the cosmos. Galaxies and stars are not fixed in place; they are moving away from each other in a coordinated, measurable pattern. This was not speculation it was a conclusion drawn from precise observational evidence that reshaped modern cosmology.)
