261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 85 0 R
/T (Finally, there is a nuclear fingerprint written into the matter around us. Calculations based on the Big Bang model predict that roughly 75% of the visible matter in the universe is hydrogen, while helium makes up about 25%, with trace amounts of lithium and heavier elements \)Peebles, 1966; Wagoner et al, 1967. These predictions were later confirmed through observations of stars, nebulae, and precise measurements from satellites such as WMAP and Planck, which studied the Cosmic Microwave Background in remarkable detail \(Planck Collaboration, 2018\). The observed ratios match exactly what Big Bang nucleo synthesis calculations predict a perfect agreement between theory and observation. This alignment confirms that the universe began in a hot, dense state and has been expanding ever since.)
/E (Finally, there is a nuclear fingerprint written into the matter around us. Calculations based on the Big Bang model predict that roughly 75% of the visible matter in the universe is hydrogen, while helium makes up about 25%, with trace amounts of lithium and heavier elements \)Peebles, 1966; Wagoner et al, 1967. These predictions were later confirmed through observations of stars, nebulae, and precise measurements from satellites such as WMAP and Planck, which studied the Cosmic Microwave Background in remarkable detail \(Planck Collaboration, 2018\). The observed ratios match exactly what Big Bang nucleo synthesis calculations predict a perfect agreement between theory and observation. This alignment confirms that the universe began in a hot, dense state and has been expanding ever since.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
